# A quick local gate before anything leaves the machine: lint, typecheck and
# unit tests of the packages that differ from origin/main, plus everything that
# depends on them.
#
# The full JavaScript job (every unit test, the E2E suite, the production-build
# smokes), the WebKit editor regression, the Rust checks (cargo check, clippy,
# test, audit) and CodeQL run in CI — and since 2026-09-28 main is protected:
# it only accepts a commit whose CI is green. Work goes to a `feature/**`
# branch first (CI runs there), main follows by fast-forward once that run is
# green. Until then this hook mirrored the whole CI job locally, 30 to 75
# minutes per push on a shared machine, and parallel sessions timed each other
# out; the protection makes the local copy redundant without weakening main.
#
# This checks the WORKING TREE, not the pushed commit — with multi-file changes
# still run `git add -A` (after reviewing `git status`) so no file is left
# behind (see CI lesson from 2026-06-30, missing blockTransforms.ts).
# The full suite locally, when wanted: `pnpm lint && pnpm typecheck && pnpm run test:all`.
pnpm turbo run lint typecheck test --filter="...[origin/main]"
